[
  {"lesson": "m-brick-kiln (Sentinel-2, 64px, 2 classes): a 2-minute screen with ssl4eo_s2 weights, all bands, flip+rot90 and CE already reached 0.985-0.990 val accuracy. The ResNet50 and ResNet18 at 128px (both 0.990) tied at the top. The spread across six configs was only 0.005, so rung 1 barely separates them. Don't spend a large explore share on this task.", "tags": ["sentinel-2", "classification", "m-brick-kiln"]},
  {"lesson": "m-brick-kiln: ssl4eo_s2 ResNet50 (lr 3e-4, wd 0.01, bs 64, CE, flip+rot90) went from 0.990 at 2 min to 0.991 at 5 min. The 3-seed mean was 0.990 ± 0.0017 (seeds scored 0.991, 0.991, 0.988). One seed lands about 0.3 points below the others, so a single-run difference under about 0.002 is noise.", "tags": ["sentinel-2", "classification", "m-brick-kiln", "seed-noise"]},
  {"lesson": "In the 2-minute screen on m-brick-kiln, ssl4eo_s2 ResNet18 scored 0.986 and ImageNet ResNet18 scored 0.985. Focal loss (0.985) and lr 2e-3 (0.986) did not beat CE at lr 5e-4. The 1-point differences are within noise. SSL4EO weights are a safe default, but the evidence for them over ImageNet is weak.", "tags": ["sentinel-2", "classification", "weights", "loss", "m-brick-kiln"]},
  {"lesson": "On m-brick-kiln, ensembling 2-3 ResNet50 seeds (0.991) and 8-view TTA (0.990 for a single run and for the 3-seed ensemble) did not beat the single best run (0.991). All are within the 0.0017 seed noise. When the single model is saturated near 0.99, skip the ensemble and TTA step and register the single run.", "tags": ["sentinel-2", "classification", "ensemble", "tta", "m-brick-kiln"]}
]
